# Astro loads this into every Airflow container automatically. Not the same
# file as the gitlake repo root .env (that one holds secrets and is mounted
# read-only into the scheduler separately).
#
# JWT expiration bumped again, 1 hour to 4 hours: 3600s covered
# stream_ingest (10-20 min) but not to_delta once its sink became
# foreachBatch + MERGE INTO -- MERGE cost scales with target table size, not
# batch size, so a full-day reprocess against an already-5.5M-row table took
# ~110 minutes and outran even the first bump. Same failure shape as before:
# the subprocess itself was fine, it lost contact with the API server
# mid-run and got torn down (SIGTERM, "Connection pool shut down") once its
# token expired. 4 hours is deliberately generous headroom, not a tight fit
# to the observed 110 minutes -- this cost will keep growing as more days
# accumulate in the target table.
AIRFLOW__API_AUTH__JWT_EXPIRATION_TIME=14400
AIRFLOW__EXECUTION_API__JWT_EXPIRATION_TIME=14400
